<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Nan of Zhou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 314–256 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Nan of Zhou was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a>, reigning from 314 to 256 BCE. By his time royal power was nominal, and he lived under the protection of the Duchy of Western Zhou. In 256 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> took the royal domain and King Nan died, ending some eight centuries of Zhou kingship.</p></div>
